beginning with a bang the Edinburgh  Fringe Festival a month of Arts and  Culture capturing the zeitgeist and  holding up a mirror to society the show  conspiracy is a study in how facts can  be unpicked if you sound convincing  enough inspired by the statistic that 60  percent of Britons believe in at least  one conspiracy theory the sort of first  came to me as something positive and  realizing that we had a conspiracy  theorist in chief in the White House  felt like a sort of instigator but I  think as we've just as we've dug into it  more it's become it's become bigger and  it's not just about the sort of people  who we think might be sat online on  reddit you know spouting things about  the moon and actually we all in all of  us have this propensity for wanting to  believe in something that perhaps  doesn't seem immediately real audiences  in Edinburgh seem drawn to performances  about how truths are manipulated and  capitalized on it osmond Baig a former  news producer plays an ambitious  journalist in his sold-out show fake  news where the audience play his in  terms what I wanted to do is to show  people what the media is really like  what a newsroom is really like exactly  how it operates kind of warts and all  but show people that it's not some sort  of there's no conspiracy theories here  you know it's not there's no agenda that  is being pushed it's not some sort of  people in an ivory tower who are  disconnected from the public it's  ordinary people trying to do their jobs  trying to do the best they can it's a  cautionary tale energetically exploring  how journalists can make innocent  mistakes these festival goers will be  able to explore every facet of fake news  at this year's fringe from false  information to genuine error through to  foreign interference one show will even  teach audiences how to dismantle false  claims with logic  orson welles infamous radio play war of  the worlds' also gets an update for the  digital age the drama allegedly caused  mass panic in America in 1938 but its  effects were exaggerated like so many  examples today just fake news born from  fiction Charley Angela al-jazeera  Edinburgh
 

